    "created_at": "2021-03-17T21:51:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-17T21:51:57Z",
    "body": "Thanks for bringing this up. I think the issue is going to be the slippery slope argument - you're arguing for the same height, but what about the rest? What about width, font, border styles, background colors, etc. It's possible I'm missing the point about why it's natural for a `<select>` to match a `<button>` when both have `appearance:none`.\r\n\r\nChromium has made changes in the past (most notably in M83) that changed the layout ever-so-slightly for several form controls, and there was a definite set of compat issues. Many sites, it seems, hard code dependencies on the UA stylesheet, particularly around sizes. So changes can break things.\r\n\r\nI'm not against changing things, if there is a clear improvement to be made, and ideally if *all* such changes can be made together.\r\n\r\ncc @gregwhitworth @zcorpan ",
