    "created_at": "2021-03-17T22:58:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-17T23:01:13Z",
    "body": "> I think the issue is going to be the slippery slope argument - you're arguing for the same height, but what about the rest? What about width, font, border styles, background colors, etc.\r\n\r\nIdeally all form controls should behave similarly across browsers when unthemed, including all those. Perhaps all the colors shouldn't _need_ to match exactly, but which properties get set from the UA sheet at least seems like a reasonable expectation from an author.\r\n\r\n> It's possible I'm missing the point about why it's natural for a `<select>` to match a `<button>` when both have appearance:none.\r\n\r\nBecause comboboxes behave and get styled like buttons, generally (modulo the arrow marker etc). That might be less true on macOS, but at least Firefox has had code in the UA sheet trying to make comboboxes / buttons / input the same height since forever.\r\n\r\n> Chromium has made changes in the past (most notably in M83) that changed the layout ever-so-slightly for several form controls, and there was a definite set of compat issues. Many sites, it seems, hard code dependencies on the UA stylesheet, particularly around sizes. So changes can break things.\r\n\r\nYeah, agreed. Exactly because of this dependency on sites on the UA sheet, this UA sheet should probably match across browsers.\r\n\r\n> I'm not against changing things, if there is a clear improvement to be made, and ideally if all such changes can be made together.\r\n\r\nI fully agree.",
